cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use voiage, please cite the v3.1.0 software release and the JOSS paper when published."
title: "voiage: Value of Information Analysis"
type: software
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
authors:
  - family-names: Mordaunt
    given-names: Dylan
    email: voiage@users.noreply.github.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9775-0603
repository-code: https://github.com/edithatogo/voiage
url: https://edithatogo.github.io/voiage
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  voiage provides Value of Information analysis through a hybrid Rust and
  Python implementation. Rust owns selected stable kernels and shared result
  contracts; Python owns the broader interface and method paths. R and Julia
  source packages expose native EVPI and ENBS; R bundles its offline Rust kernel.
keywords:
  - value of information
  - decision analysis
  - health economics
  - uncertainty quantification
